{"reference":"Psalms 132","book":"Psalms","chapter":132,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Among the Songs of Ascents","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Psalm 132 belongs within Psalms 120–134, a group that includes Songs of Ascents oriented toward worship. Within the wider Psalter, communal psalms also preserve memories of sanctuary destruction and Babylonian exile alongside thanksgiving for return and festival praise. This broader setting may help frame the psalm’s focus on Zion, worship, and the ark, though the precise relationship remains debated.","verse_refs":["Psalms 120:1-7","Psalms 121:1-8","Psalms 122:1-9","Psalms 123:1-4","Psalms 124:1-8","Psalms 125:1-5","Psalms 126:1-6","Psalms 127:1-5","Psalms 128:1-6","Psalms 129:1-8","Psalms 130:1-8","Psalms 131:1-3","Psalms 133:1-3","Psalms 134:1-3"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_132_c247f3354d7b8540538a65aa"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}